- Story & Context: Brother Silas accidentally calibrated his dream-oscillator to the monastery's iron gate, causing the latch to moan with a pitch that fractured the chapel stained glass as the clock struck noon. "Everything waits but the iron teeth," he hummed as the rhythm shifted into a violent, percussive landslide of screeching oscillators.
